
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

## test_menu — host-side tests for the generated menu logic

`test_menu/test_menu_logic.c` pins down the behaviour of the **generated**
menu module (`src/menu/`, produced by MenuCraft): navigation, the edit state
machine, value clamping/wrapping and the event callbacks the app layer
(`hipims_menu_glue.c`) relies on. The menu module is pure C (no hardware), so
it runs on any host.

### Build & run with any C99 compiler

Verified on WSL (gcc 13.3):

```bash
cd /mnt/d/Projects/PlatformIO/HiPIMS_Menu

gcc -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Isrc/menu/include -Iinclude \
    test/test_menu/test_menu_logic.c \
    src/menu/menu.c src/menu/menu_context.c src/menu/menu_data_config.c \
    src/menu/menu_data_context.c src/menu/menu_data_name.c \
    src/menu/menu_data_tree.c src/menu/menu_data_value.c \
    src/menu/menu_draw.c src/menu/menu_edit.c src/menu/menu_name.c \
    src/menu/menu_navigate.c src/menu/menu_value_access.c \
    -o /tmp/test_menu_logic && /tmp/test_menu_logic
```

Exit code = number of failed checks (0 = all passed).

Notes:
- The test replaces the app callbacks (`hipims_*`) with recording stubs — the
  generated `menu_data_config.c` registers them as function pointers.
- The only compiler warning comes from the generated `menu_reset()` (unused
  `ctx`); generated code is intentionally not edited.
- If the PlatformIO `unity` framework is ever installed, this test can be
  wired into `pio test -e native` (add `[env:native]` with
  `platform = native`, `build_src_filter = +<menu/*>` and the two `-I` flags);
  the assert helpers already mirror unity's `TEST_ASSERT_*` checks.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
